  "body": "Install a repository tagged magpie-plugin by its GitHub URL or a git URL, and its card on the Plugins page says Installed but never Sign in, though the plugin has a provider to sign in to. The Installed tab's row does offer it.\n\nactionFor reads a card's sign-ins by the card's own spec: subsOf(pkg) keeps the providers.plugins whose name(x.spec) is pkg (plugins.js:89 and 474; lines at f8cd964a). A tagged repository's card is github:owner/repo, or npm's name when npm has the package from that repository, while entryOf finds the installed plugin by whichever spec names that repository (75-79): its page's URL on main, and with the patch I'm posting on #3685 also git+https, git+ssh and git:// URLs. The Installed tab's row reads by the entry's own spec, name(e.spec) (1116-1117), so it shows them. actionFor could read them the same way, subsOf(name(e.spec)) for the entry it found.\n\nI checked it on the page with a faked API in Chromium and WebKit: installed by its URL or by a git+https URL, the card says Installed with no Sign in, and the Installed tab's row offers Sign in. Not tried in the app.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
