   "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:19:11Z",
   "body": "The card read installed but offered no Sign in because `actionFor` looked up the plugin's providers by the card's own package (`subsOf(pkg)`), while a tagged repository's card is named `github:owner/repo` (or npm's name) and the installed entry and its provider are named by the spec it was installed with — the repository's page URL, or a `git+` URL. The Installed tab's row reads by the entry's own spec (`name(e.spec)`), which is why it worked there.\n\nThe branch resolves the installed entry first and reads `subsOf(name(e.spec))` and `movableOf(name(e.spec))`, the same way the Installed row does, so the card offers Sign in for a repository installed by its URL or a git URL.\n\n[fix/3930-gui-a-repository-s-card](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3930-gui-a-repository-s-card), commit dc9212d2b5ac1d1473a267bdf44af31720417846\n\nRun at that head: the new `internal/gui/tests/plugin-git-url-signin.test.cjs` failed on the unmodified code (`expected 'Installed' to be 'Sign in'`) and passes now on Chromium and WebKit; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/gui/`, `go test ./internal/gui/ -count=1` (459 tests) and the plugin-page Playwright tests (32 pass) are green. `plugin-github.test.cjs`'s 440px \"a click scrolls nothing\" assertion fails the same way on clean `upstream/main`, so it is not from this change.\n\nThis is a fork branch, ready for review; it makes no claim on the issue's ownership.\n",
